-- ============================================================================
-- SC4 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Offshore & Marine Logistics, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/marine/intermediate.
--
-- What this tier owns: FLEET SIZING AND DECK PLANNING. Demand over a period and
-- what drives the voyage count; voyages rounded up or kept as the average,
-- voyage days and vessel-days; available days, the vessel rounding rule, spare
-- and short vessel-days; deck cargo footprints, the area bound and the lower
-- bound; first-fit decreasing and first fit in the booked order; the
-- published packing examples.
--
-- AN APP COURSE. The Suite app is the Marine Logistics Planner; the practicals
-- also run in the course's own voyage and fleet calculator and deck
-- calculator. The capstone grades six values of this tier, each identical under
-- every reading the engine states and never a Monte Carlo draw.
-- ============================================================================

values ('marine', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-demand-over-a-period","title":"Demand over a Period","lesson_keys":["l01-weekly-demand-per-installation","l02-demand-over-capacity-per-constraint","l03-minimum-visits","l04-what-drives-the-voyage-count"]},{"key":"m02-voyages-and-vessel-days","title":"Voyages and Vessel-Days","lesson_keys":["l01-rounding-voyages-up-or-not-at-all","l02-voyage-days-and-vessel-days","l03-dedicated-voyages-sized-one-by-one","l04-a-voyage-longer-than-the-days-available"]},{"key":"m03-vessels-required","title":"Vessels Required","lesson_keys":["l01-available-days-and-the-period","l02-rounding-vessels","l03-spare-and-short-vessel-days","l04-fleet-utilisation-and-fuel-for-the-period","l05-a-psv-or-an-ahts-for-the-same-demand"]},{"key":"m04-deck-cargo-and-footprints","title":"Deck Cargo and Footprints","lesson_keys":["l01-items-footprints-and-units","l02-the-area-bound-with-no-stacking","l03-the-lower-bound-on-voyages","l04-what-the-area-bound-leaves-out"]},{"key":"m05-first-fit-decreasing","title":"First-Fit Decreasing","lesson_keys":["l01-sorting-by-area","l02-the-first-voyage-that-holds-a-unit","l03-ties-go-to-the-heavier-unit","l04-first-fit-in-the-booked-order","l05-overflow-and-its-reasons"]},{"key":"m06-published-packing-examples","title":"Published Packing Examples","lesson_keys":["l01-two-capacities-one-list","l02-when-a-larger-deck-needs-more-voyages","l03-a-tight-worst-case","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
